{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 39, "model_name": "nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b", "content": "**A Whirlwind Week in Japan**\n\nLanding in Tokyo felt like stepping into a living neon dream. After a quick ramen slurp at a tiny stall near Shibuya Crossing, I dove into the city’s pulse: wandering the serene Meiji Shrine, sipping matcha in Harajuku’s hidden cafés, and losing track of time among the endless shelves of Akihabara’s electronic wonderland.\n\nThe bullet train whisked me to Kyoto, where ancient temples greeted me with quiet grace. I spent sunrise at Fushimi Inari, threading through thousands of vermilion torii gates that seemed to stretch into eternity. In the afternoon, I joined a tea ceremony in a centuries‑old machiya house, feeling the deliberate calm of each whisked motion. Evenings were spent strolling Gion’s lantern‑lit alleys, hoping for a glimpse of a geisha hurrying to her next appointment.\n\nA day trip to Nara rewarded me with friendly deer bowing for crackers and the awe‑inspiring Todaiji Buddha, its bronze visage radiating timeless serenity. Finally, I headed north to Hakone, where an onsen ryokan offered steaming baths overlooking Mount Fuji’s snow‑capped silhouette—a perfect, soothing farewell.\n\nJapan’s blend of hyper‑modern energy and deep‑rooted tradition left me humming with inspiration, already plotting my next return.", "logprobs": [{"token": "We", "logprob": -0.1437203288078308}, {"token": " need", "logprob": -0.003130299737676978}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.08303068578243256}, {"token": " output", "logprob": -2.1139800548553467}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.021854175254702568}, {"token": " short", "logprob": -0.0024947968777269125}, {"token": " blog", "logprob": -3.4570634852570947e-06}, {"token": " post", "logprob": -0.00010752100206445903}, {"token": " about", "logprob": -0.5659010410308838}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0002127659390680492}, {"token": " trip", "logprob": -6.758938252460212e-05},